From 5b8568353e747dba42f67d318bc4fecae39042bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vuln Patch Pipeline <vuln-patch@chainguard.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:29:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Confine admin stub file deletes to the __files root

DeleteStubFileTask, which serves DELETE /__admin/files/{filename},
built a File from the files root and the raw filename and deleted it
with no containment check (CWE-22). On Windows a backslash in the
filename acts as a path separator, so a name that starts with "..\"
deleted a file outside the __files root.

The task now deletes through FileSource.deleteFile, which checks that
the canonical path is under the root and throws NotAuthorisedException
if it is not. AbstractFileSource.deleteFile also refuses a name that
resolves to the root directory itself, such as "" or ".". The task
reports a refused delete as its existing 500 "File not deleted"
response, and returns 200 only when the target existed before the call
and is gone after it. A delete on a read-only file source now fails,
as other writes to it already did. A delete on a classpath file source
leaves the file in place, since ClasspathFileSource.deleteFile does
nothing.

AbstractFileSource.assertFilePathIsUnderRoot compared canonical paths
with a bare startsWith, so a sibling directory whose name starts with
the root's name, such as __files-archive next to __files, passed the
check. The check now accepts only the root itself or a path under the
root followed by a separator. Reads, writes and deletes through
AbstractFileSource use this check.

Deletes of files and empty directories inside the root, and reads and
writes inside the root, are unchanged.

Adds DeleteStubFileTaskTest, DeleteStubFileTaskPathTraversalTest,
DeleteStubFileTaskEdgeCaseTest, DeleteStubFileHttpTest.

Cgp-Finding: CGP-48gv-xfgw-w4hc
